title: Migration to V1.0
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

!! Breaking changes from v0.x

v1.0.0-beta-1 moves from a hardcoded 9-glyph alphabet to a data-driven [[Vocabulary Engine]] of marker tiddlers. Existing pragma usage keeps working via a bridge, but a few defaults have changed.

!! Removed glyphs

`´` (tick), `≈` (approx) and `¶` (pilcrow) are no longer in Vocab/Default. Opt back in by adding `;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs` to the tiddler's type field:

''Before''

```
title: my-tiddler
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

´.bigger Welcome
```

''After''

```
title: my-tiddler
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs

´.bigger Welcome
```

!! Block-marker termination

`°` (degree) and `›` (single) now default to ''blank-line'' termination. Back-to-back `°foo` `°bar` lines join into one block.

To restore the v0.x single-newline behaviour, use `_mode=inline`:

```
\custom degree=foo _mode=inline
```

Or set `mode: inline` directly on the marker tiddler. Note: `_endString="\n"` does ''not'' work; TW's pragma parser keeps `\n` as two literal characters.

!! `\custom <kind>=<symbol>` still works

The legacy pragma path bridges through each marker's `legacy-kind` field. `\custom tick=foo _element=em` still registers `foo` as a symbol on the `´` marker. v0.x pragma-driven tiddlers continue to work once their vocab is activated.

!! Dropped plugin dependency

`pragma-comment` is no longer a dependency. HTML comments live in TW core.

!! Editor toolbar dropdowns

From v1.0.0-beta-2, the prefix and inline-glyph dropdowns filter their radios by the active vocabulary for the tiddler being edited. New vocabularies appear automatically in the dropdown without code changes.

